   "text": {
    "L1": "A polygon is a closed shape made only of straight sides.",
    "L2": "First check for a gap, then check that every side is straight.",
    "L3": "Count the sides to name the polygon: three is a triangle, four a quadrilateral, and five a pentagon.",
    "L4": "Six sides make a hexagon, and eight sides make an octagon.",
    "L5": "Turning, flipping, or stretching does not change a shape's name if its number of sides stays the same.",
    "L6": "A triangle does not need a flat, horizontal base. It still has three straight sides and three corners.",
    "L7": "A tilted closed shape with five straight sides is a pentagon, even when its sides have different lengths.",
    "L8": "Now tap the shape that is a polygon."
   },
